course: dictionary
lesson: 10780
title: Trying in vain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Vainly» means without success. When you do something vainly, you try hard, but it does not work. Look for the clue in the sentence: did the effort get a result? If not, the word is probably «vainly».
explain: The same idea is in the phrase «in vain», which means with no result. «I called her name in vain» means I called, but she did not hear or come. In «Alice tries vainly to reach the key on the glass table», the clue is that she is trying to reach something, so the sentence is about effort that fails.
explain: «Vainly» has a second, less common meaning: in a proud way about your looks or abilities. Both meanings are about trying or showing off, so the rest of the sentence tells you which one it is. Read the words around it first.
fact: «Vainly» means without success, or in vain.
fact: «In vain» means with no result, as in «She knocked in vain».
fact: «Vainly tried» means tried hard but did not succeed.
fact: «The Rat had vainly tried to shield him» means the Rat tried to protect him, but it did not work.
fact: The less common meaning of «vainly» is in a proud way about your looks or abilities.
exercise: «He tried vainly to open the door.» What does vainly mean here? | Without success, so the door stayed shut | Very loudly and quickly | In a kind and gentle way | *Without success, so the door stayed shut, and he kept trying
exercise: «Mole searches vainly for the path in the Wild Wood.» What happens to Mole? | He finds the path straight away | He does not find the path | He is given a map by a friend | *He searches, but he does not find the path
exercise: Which phrase means with no result? | In all its fullness | *In vain | Once again | Right away
test: Which word means the same as «vainly» in «the Rat had vainly tried to shield him»? | Quietly | Successfully | *Unsuccessfully | Bravely
test: Lily says, «She vainly admired her new hat in the mirror.» What does vainly suggest? | Very quietly | *In a proud way, pleased with her looks | Without success | Sadly, with tears
exam: Which sentence uses vainly in the less common sense of proud about looks? | Ben vainly searched the bag for his keys | *Ben vainly stood at the mirror, admiring his new haircut | Ben vainly shouted for help in the snow | Ben vainly checked the lock all night
